trols, investment screening, industrial policy, currency and financial power, and infrastructure financing","Appreciate the concept of weaponised interdependence, and how network centrality (in finance, technology and supply chains) confers coercive power on some states and vulnerability on others","Examine how India navigates a geoeconomic world: balancing openness and strategic autonomy, de-risking from China, and leveraging its market size","Evaluate the limits of geoeconomic coercion: when do sanctions and embargoes work, and when do they backfire?"],"mandatory":[{"id":"pp223_lu03_m01","url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/18lqes7LKbxy3vJn6J5sCiwWrCs43EHCv/view?usp=sharing","desc":"Henry Farrell and Abraham Newman","name":"Weaponized Interdependence: How Global Economic Networks Shape State Coercion"},{"id":"pp223_lu03_m02","url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UcGauCTVrA2_-g0mC13ZMgQZE39Ifgeo/view?usp=sharing","desc":"Edward Luttwak","name":"From Geopolitics to Geo-Economics: Logic of Conflict, Grammar of Commerce"}],"selfStudy":false,"recommended":[{"id":"pp223_lu03_r01","url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rSEr5yddEFdUbvNS4lwFIxruX1RJmL3Z/view?usp=sharing","desc":"Jennifer Harris and Robert Blackwill (Introduction + Ch. 1, \"What is Geoeconomics?\")","name":"War by Other Means: Geoeconomics and Statecraft"},{"id":"pp223_lu03_r02","url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qs07zm_YVRHvvznMfYU7r7TQ28ol6NiE/view?usp=drive_link","desc":"Glenn Diesen (Chapters 2 & 4)","name":"Great Power Politics in the Fourth Industrial Revolution: The Geoeconomics of Technological Sovereignty"},{"id":"pp223_lu03_r03","url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yfihhGWFbSpbLEigCz1ZKLmQksXuuVa7/view?usp=sharing","desc":"Sanjaya Baru","name":"India and the World: Economics and Politics of the Manmohan Singh Doctrine in Foreign Policy"}]}],"code":"International Relations","icon":"🌍","name":"PP223: International Relations and Foreign Affairs","color":"#267336"}$pp$::jsonb as s, 0::num